Goal

Define the architecture of the Amazon Rufus AI clone by detailing the Planner Agent’s role, responsibilities, and tools.
The Planner Agent coordinates other agents to fulfill user requests in a conversational and reliable way.

Planner Agent
Role

The orchestrator: interprets user intent, builds a step-by-step plan, and coordinates other agents.

Responsibilities

Ask the user for clarification if intent is ambiguous.

Generate a draft execution plan and present it for approval.

Invoke the right agents in sequence to fulfill the request.

Combine outputs into a final user-friendly response.

Report success or gracefully handle errors.

Tools

Pre-curated Plans Repository (templates for common queries).

Agent Invocation Framework (trigger other agents as “tools”).

User Interaction Layer (clarifications, approvals, corrections).

Example Flow

User:
“Is there a hardcover?”

Steps:

Planner Agent receives query.

Planner Agent recognizes the request as a product variant lookup.

Planner Agent invokes the Product Information Agent.

Product Information Agent fetches available formats.

Planner Agent collects the result and confirms hardcover availability.

Response returned to the user:
“Yes, there is a hardcover available.”
